. *********************************
. *** Apply sample restrictions ***
. *********************************
. 
. * We estimate the following regressions using a sample restricted to responde
> nts with exactly one child.
. * Note: There was a typo in the preliminary Stata code provided in the PAP. A
> lthough the verbal description 
. * of the sample restriction was correct, the code mistakenly included `parity
> 2==1`, which would select 
. * respondents with at least two children—contradicting the intended analytic 
> sample.
. 
. 
. keep if parity2!=1 // Hypotheses 1, 2, 3, 4
(10,999 observations deleted)

. 
. * Restrict the analyses to cohabiting couples 
. *keep if cohab==1 // Hypothesis 3
. 
. keep if !missing(female, educ , birthyear, phrf) & phrf!=0
(7,117 observations deleted)

. keep if !missing(famvscareer) | !missing(menhousework)
(17,008 observations deleted)

